t": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 17}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "•       on the (18) _________________ foot", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "blank", "offset": 962, "answer": {"text": "left", "source": {"id": "offline-1ab9dee1df3429db4453", "filename": "TEST ONE.pdf", "sha256": "1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 17}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "•       Swelling radiates across toes towards (19) _________________ of foot", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "blank", "offset": 1069, "answer": {"text": "the outside / outside", "source": {"id": "offline-1ab9dee1df3429db4453", "filename": "TEST ONE.pdf", "sha256": "1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 17}}, {"number": 21, "prompt": "•       Swelling settled within (21) ________________", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "blank", "offset": 1390}, {"number": 22, "prompt": "•       Ongoing (22) ________________ in toe", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "blank", "offset": 1461}, {"number": 23, "prompt": "•       Suspected (23) _______________", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "blank", "offset": 1540}, {"number": 24, "prompt": "•       Clinical Decision: (24) ________________ with current medications", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "blank", "offset": 1817}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["393d34a0620518b365c16575602f34143381e254fa17afbfa5dfe952c4c14374"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-1ab9dee1df3429db4453", "filename": "TEST ONE.pdf", "sha256": "1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [17]}], "passages": []}, {"id": "1ab9dee1df3429db-p10", "label": "Part C · TEST ONE.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215", "pages": [10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16], "questions": [{"number": 31, "prompt": "What is Dr Cristine Ericson’s opinion about fasting before blood tests?\nA        It is not supported by scientific evidence.\nB        It is superior to non-fasting blood tests.\nC        It\nIt is\nis supported\nsupported by\nby convention\nconvention not\nnot data\ndata.\nIt is supported by convention not data", "sourcePage": 12, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 540}, {"number": 32, "prompt": "What does Dr Cristine Ericson say about the research on non-fasting blood tests?\nA      The majority comes from Copenhagen.\nB      More studies should focus on children.\nC      It includes data from multiple countries.", "sourcePage": 12, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1161}, {"number": 33, "prompt": "What is Dr Cristine Ericson’s opinion on the difference between the results of fasting and\nnon-fasting tests?\nA      The small differences are unimportant.\nB      There is no difference in the results.\nC      There is a small but significant difference.\n[CANDIDATE NO.] LISTENING QUESTION PAPER 3/12", "sourcePage": 12, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1430}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "According to Dr Cristine Ericson, why are non-fasting blood tests popular with the public?\nA      Because of the strong research evidence in the report.\nB      Because of positive publicity in the newspaper and on TV.\nC      Because they are more convenient for busy lifestyles.", "sourcePage": 13, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 400}, {"number": 36, "prompt": "Which of the following statements best summarises Dr Cristine Ericson’s position on the\nuse of fasting or non-fasting blood tests?\nA      In rare cases fasting before a blood test is necessary.\nB      Fasting before a blood test should no longer be recommended.\nC      New research is needed on the use of fasting and non-fasting tests.\nNow look at extract two.\n[CANDIDATE NO.] LISTENING QUESTION PAPER 4/12", "sourcePage": 13, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 729}, {"number": 38, "prompt": "According to Dr Patrecivich, how will wearable sensors and smartphones help GPs?\nA      They will allow doctors mobility to visit patients in remote locations.\nB      They will allow doctors to check if patients are following their advice.\nC      They will allow doctors to monitor their patients with real-time data.", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 511}, {"number": 40, "prompt": "According to the talk, both sports medicine and oncology\nA      will use technology to make their processes faster and cheaper.\nB      will use technology to filter data and individualise therapy.\nC      will use technology like Xbox to treat patients from a distance.", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0}, {"number": 41, "prompt": "What does Dr Patrecivich suggest about the effect of technology on cancer treatment?\nA      Artificial intelligence technology will eventually cure cancer.\nB      Oncologists will keep patients informed using social media.\nC      Technology will have a powerful and positive effect on oncology.", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 318}, {"number": 42, "prompt": "What is Dr Patrecivich’s conclusion about the future of medicine and technology?\nA      Medical technology will give doctors more time and better data to care for patients.\nB      Physicians will have amazing opportunities to develop new medical technologies.\nC      Automated and robotic systems will gradually replace humans in medical practice.\nThat is the end of Part C.\nYou now have two minutes to check your answers.\nTHAT IS THE END OF THE LISTENING TEST\n[CANDIDATE NO.] LISTENING QUESTION PAPER 6/12", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 663}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["393d34a0620518b365c16575602f34143381e254fa17afbfa5dfe952c4c14374"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-1ab9dee1df3429db4453", "filename": "TEST ONE.pdf", "sha256": "1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/1ab9dee1df3429db44531a92d08a108a10854a2f1646cfeb972a66c060163215.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [17]}], "passages": []}]}
